            <div xml:id="d491">

                <pb facs="0580" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/1077: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-23T15:00:00-04:00">May 23, 1936—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>125. Your 254, May 23, 1 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Has there been press comment in regard to the measures of monetary reform
                        and the statements of May 18 made by Kung and the United States Treasury
                        Department? If so, please summarize.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Please amplify statements that “Kung’s statement is confusing and
                        unnecessarily disturbing” and that “the psychological effect has been
                        bad”.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Reports from Hankow and Shanghai indicate that the measures of monetary
                        reform were well received there.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Report promptly by radio.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
